  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The free body diagram of block + tube inclusive of water is as shown. Since the block + tube system shown in figure is in equilibrium.<br /><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi></math> Net weight of system = buoyant fore<br /><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/Ammamama.PNG\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 156px;\" /></p><p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>&nbsp;be the volume of the block, then<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>v</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfrac><mi>l</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mi>&#160;</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>g</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>l</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math><br /><br />or <math><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mrow><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p>",
